-- title:
--   Level automorphisms normalise the Γ(q) subgroup and its fixed field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of `levelH q M'`, the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ along $\ell \mid q^2M'$. Let $K \subseteq L((T))$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion field `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`. Let $G$ be the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ generated by all $\tau$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ — that is, $\tau$ transforms every quotient $f/g$ of weight-$k$ modular forms for [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) with integral $q$-expansions, read in $K$, into the corresponding quotient of the slash actions by the conjugated matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` after transporting coefficients along $\iota$ — and let $K_0 = K^G$. Then for any $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and any $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`: $\tau\sigma\tau^{-1} \in G$ and $\tau^{-1}\sigma\tau \in G$ for all $\sigma \in G$, and both $\tau$ and $\tau^{-1}$ map $K_0$ into itself.
--
--   This is the normalisation statement underlying the classical description of the action of $\Gamma_0(M')$ on the function fields of modular curves of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$: the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ conjugate the subgroup coming from $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ into itself, hence descend to the fixed field $K_0$. It is used by the auxiliary diamond-operator lemmas on rigid charts and supersingular invariants, where automorphisms of $K$ must be pushed down to $K_0$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevelOne_mul_mul_inv_mem_and_map_fixedField_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma0_of_dvd.lean

